  "verdict": {
    "text": "Iran, Islamic Rep. pledges a 4% reduction by 2030 against 2030 business-as-usual. 48 observed values are loaded from DS-02 (11), DS-35 (35), DS-40 (2). For 2024 the sources disagree: DS-02 1237.3 MtCO₂e, DS-35 1012.2 MtCO₂e. They are on different inventory scopes and the engine does not reconcile them. No implementation gap is reported: the pledge is 4% below a business-as-usual projection for 2030. That projection is not in any source loaded here, so the percentage cannot be turned into a tonnage and the trend cannot be judged against it. ND-GAIN scores it 47.5 for 2024. In the first NDC round, WRI's CAIT assessment recorded: 4% (unconditional) up to 12% (conditional) reduction in GHG emissions by 2030 compared to the BAU scenario It was classed both. That is a 2016 assessment of an earlier submission, not the target above. Projected warming for 2080-2099 against 1995-2014 ranges from +1.59°C under SSP1-2.6 to +5.62°C under SSP5-8.5. These are model runs, not observations.",
